SPOILERS FOLLOW!








































  It's a difficult question since what I wish for depends on what type of 
character I'm playing and how advanced the character is when I get the wish.

  Although several posters have already posted most of the choice items to
wish for there are a few more that I would add. I consider the first ten
levels or so to be the most difficult part of the game and my suggestions 
are based on a low level character getting a wish. In order of least to 
most useful: 

  Blessed +3 helm of opposite alignment. Nice item if you're playing a priest,
  say, and want Stormbringer or Mjollnir. Very convenient for converting
  an altar to lawful or chaotic to get holy or unholy water respectively. 

  Blessed +3 cloak of invisibility. Invisibility is a very powerful intrinsic
  in the first levels since most monsters can't see invisible. Better than a 
  ring since you don't burn food. Also better than a blessed potion of 
  invisibility since you can become visible to enter shops.

  A blessed figurine of a jabberwock. Gives a tame pet of the same type as the 
  figurine. Some other nice pets: purple worm, cockatrice, dragon, minotaur,
  Olog-hai etc.
  
  Blessed magic marker. Very useful for enchanting your weapon to maximum.

  My favorite wish - a blessed athame (assuming you're playing something
  other than a wizard). This is a terrific item for surviving the first
  levels, especially nasties such as rothe packs and worse - killer bees
  and soldier ants.

  And, of course, Stormbringer, Mjollnir, or a ring of conflict are some
  of my other favorite wishes.


  Some comments on your list:

   I never wish for Excalibur since it's easy to get it from a fountain 
(and rust-proof to boot!). I prefer to wish for Stormbringer or Mjollnir.

  I always wish for a wand of polymorph rather than gray dragon scale mail
since I can always count on finding a gray dragon somewhere in the game. 
GDSM is nice for it's magic resistance properties but it's usually not too
difficult to simply avoid magic using monsters until you find a gray dragon.

  Helm of telepathy is nice but not really necessary for survival, I wouldn't 
wish for one in the first levels.

  Gauntlets of power are a nice wish if you're playing a wizard or priest with
strength of 8. Speed boots are worth a wish at any stage of the game. I would, 
however, never wish for gauntlets of power if I'm playing a strong character 
(barbarian, caveman, valkyrie etc.).

  I try to avoid using wands of death as they are simply too dangerous. They're
also ineffective against undead.

  Cloak of displacement is a nice wish for a character who already has intrinsic
invisibility and GDSM. For a low level character I would prefer a cloak of 
invisibility. The shield of reflection is also a very nice item since it's 
rust proof and you can forget about colliding with floating eyes. It's also
nice for protection from monsters with breath weapons. But again, more suitable
as a wish for a high level character.

  Scrolls of genocide are nice but I normally wouldn't wish for them. Especially
since you may ask for three but get only one. If I haven't found any scrolls of genocide by the castle level I might consider wishing for them but such games 
are rare.

  A blessed luckstone is worth a wish at any stage of the game.



